{
  "_comment": "SHARED name-conflict modal (scenes/shared/ — Aaron 2026-08-14 ruling 2A3592D0; catalog review B05B3D09 §4c). LIFTED from the Quartermaster's inline `qm_prompt` subtree, which was mouse-only (QoL 49307EC7 #4: its three buttons and its checkbox carried no `tab_group`/`nav_ordinal`, so a pad could never answer the question) — every control here is pad-reachable, which is the whole reason the dialog moved. The design of record is F5E9D671: the colliding name over the folder it lands in, EXISTING vs INCOMING compare cards, an `Apply to the remaining N` checkbox shown only when more than one conflict is outstanding, and Skip / Keep both / Replace. The three answers ride the SAME fixed slots every choice_dialog uses (`modal_opt_0..2`), so `SharedModal` maps them back to the caller's own action names with no bespoke channel; the checkbox rides out as the close PAYLOAD (\"1\" / \"0\"), which is what lets a caller resolve the whole batch as ONE undo entry. Esc / pad-B fold to `modal_cancel` via the root `on_cancel`, honoured only when the caller declared the modal cancellable. NO `behaviour` key (the manifest skips scenes/shared/); NO pair script (the params ARE the arrangement); chrome styles ride Main.scene.json's carrier through `main_scene_styles()`.",
