            "_comment": "NO `align` here. A row's `align` is a CROSS-AXIS instruction: anything but the default `stretch` sizes each child to its own INTRINSIC cross extent, and a `button` that names no `size` / `height` / `size_class` measures ZERO (flicker-widgets component.rs, the `button` arm of `measure`). `align: center` on this row is what made all three answers lay out 154×0 — drawn as nothing, and unreachable by pointer or pad, which is exactly what Aaron hit in-window (incident B89FAC21; the same zeroing as 10A07012). These buttons FILL the row's 44px, so the row must stretch them.",
